<title>USA: USDA seeks comment on FY98 sugar tariff-rate quota.</title>
<headline>USDA seeks comment on FY98 sugar tariff-rate quota.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday said it was seeking public comments on how to administer the raw cane sugar tariff-rate quota (TRQ) in fiscal year 1998, which begins October 1.</p>
<p>USDA said Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman proposes to continue the current TRQ plan next year but will consider public comments before making a final decision.</p>
<p>Comments should be sent by August 8 to Stephen Hammond, Sugar Group Team Leader, Foreign Agricultural Service, USDA, Stop 1021, Washington, DC 20250-1021, the department said.</p>
<p>It said a final announcement will be made on or before September 17.</p>
</text>
